    "slug": "eritrea-accuses-uae-of-colonial-port-expansion-in-africa",
    "summary": "Eritrean Foreign Minister Osman Saleh accused the UAE of pursuing a strategic and military agenda through port investments in Africa, calling it 'port colonialism' in an interview with Middle East Eye.",
    "content": "Eritrea's Foreign Minister, Osman Saleh, has publicly accused the United Arab Emirates of expanding its influence across Africa through a network of port investments. In an interview with Middle East Eye, Saleh described these actions as \"port colonialism,\" arguing that they extend beyond commercial interests to include strategic and military objectives.\n\nSaleh's remarks come amid growing concerns over the UAE's increasing presence in the Red Sea and Horn of Africa regions. He questioned why the UAE is establishing port facilities in multiple African countries, suggesting that the motivations are not purely economic. The foreign minister called on African governments to scrutinize these deals more closely.\n\nThe UAE has invested in ports and logistics infrastructure in several African nations in recent years, including in the Horn of Africa. These investments are often framed as development projects, but critics argue they can lead to long-term dependency and strategic leverage. Eritrea's accusations reflect broader unease about foreign military and economic entrenchment on the continent.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development is particularly relevant. Somalia has its own history with foreign involvement in its ports, and many in the diaspora are wary of external powers gaining strategic footholds in the region. The Red Sea corridor is vital for trade and security, and any shift in control can affect Somali interests.\n\nEritrea's stance may also influence regional dynamics, as it has previously clashed with the UAE over its military presence in the area. The Somali diaspora, which maintains close ties to the Horn of Africa, will be watching how this dispute unfolds and whether it leads to changes in port agreements or regional alliances.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/13/eritrea-oo-imaaraadka-ku-eedaysay-gumeysi-dekedeed-oo-afrika-ka-socda/",
